actions / general
  core.abort    Abort            Ends the workflow as failed
  core.check    Check Condition  Fails with a message when a condition is false
  core.dummy    Dummy            Does nothing; collects branches into one point
  core.log      Log              Writes a message to the run log
  core.start    Start            Entry point of the workflow
  core.success  Success          Ends the workflow successfully
  core.wait     Wait             Waits for a given time
actions / execution
  core.run-pipeline  Run Pipeline  Runs a pipeline with parameters; output: the counts of its transforms
  core.run-workflow  Run Workflow  Runs another workflow with parameters; output: its outputs
  core.script        JavaScript    Runs JavaScript with params; output: the value of return
  shell.powershell   PowerShell    Runs a PowerShell script with named parameters; output: exitCode, stdout, stderr and optionally JSON
  shell.run          Run Program   Starts a program with arguments, without a shell; output: exitCode, stdout and stderr
actions / files
  archive.create   Create Archive   Packs files and folders into a ZIP, TAR or TAR.GZ archive; output: path, files and size
  archive.extract  Extract Archive  Unpacks a ZIP, TAR or TAR.GZ archive into a folder; output: the unpacked files
  file.copy        Copy Files       Copies files or folders; output: the copied files
  file.delete      Delete Files     Deletes files or folders; output: the deleted paths
  file.exists      File Exists      Checks whether files or folders exist; output: the matching paths
  file.list        List Files       Lists the files of a folder; output: path, name, size, modified and folder of each entry
  file.mkdir       Create Folder    Creates a folder with its parent folders; output: the path
  file.move        Move Files       Moves files or folders; output: the new paths
  file.read        Read File        Reads a small text file into the workflow, as text, lines or JSON; output: content, value or lines, size and modified
  file.wait        Wait for File    Waits until files exist; output: the matching paths
  file.write       Write File       Writes a text or a value as JSON to a file, replacing it or appending; output: path and size
actions / network
  http.request   HTTP Request   Sends an HTTP request, e.g. to a REST API; output: status, headers and body of the answer
  http.response  HTTP Response  Answers the caller of an HTTP trigger with status, headers and body; output: sent and status
  mail.send      Send Mail      Sends a mail through a mail server, with text or HTML and attachments
actions / database
  db.execute  Execute SQL  Runs an SQL statement on a database, e.g. to insert, update or delete rows
  db.query    Query SQL    Reads the rows of an SQL query into the workflow; output: rows, count, first and value
transforms / input
  core.generate-rows  Generate Rows  Creates records with constant fields
  csv.input           CSV Input      Reads the rows of a CSV file as records
  db.table-input      Table Input    Reads the rows of an SQL query as records, one field per column
  excel.input         Excel Input    Reads the rows of a sheet of an Excel workbook (.xlsx) as records
  file.list           List Files     Reads the files of a folder as records: path, name, extension, size, modified and folder
  json.input          JSON Input     Reads the objects of a JSON or NDJSON file as records
  xml.input           XML Input      Reads the elements of an XML file as records
transforms / transform
  core.calculate      Calculate      Sets fields for every record: a copy of another field, a fixed value, a default or a calculated value
  core.constant       Add Constants  Adds fields with the same value to every record
  core.convert        Convert Types  Converts fields to another type, with a number or date format
  core.filter         Filter         Passes on the records for which a condition is true
  core.map-values     Map Values     Replaces the values of a field by a table, e.g. codes by names
  core.script         Script         Runs JavaScript for every record: return a new record, several or none
  core.select-fields  Select Fields  Keeps, orders and renames fields, or removes fields
  core.sequence       Sequence       Numbers the records in the order they arrive, also per group
  core.split-field    Split Field    Splits the text of a field into several fields or into one record per part
transforms / flow
  core.dummy   Dummy   Passes all records on unchanged
  core.switch  Switch  Passes each record to the link of the first case whose condition is true
transforms / execution
  core.from-result  Records from Workflow  Passes on the records the calling workflow gave to the pipeline (rows)
  core.to-result    Records to Workflow    Returns the records to the calling workflow (output.rows) and passes them on
transforms / combine
  core.dedupe         Remove Duplicates  Passes on the first record of each combination of values and drops repeated ones
  core.group-by       Group By           Combines records with the same values into one, with count, sum and other aggregates
  core.merge-join     Merge Join         Joins the records of two inputs sorted by the same keys, like a join in a database
  core.sort           Sort               Sorts the records by fields; keeps all records in memory
  core.stream-lookup  Stream Lookup      Adds the fields of the matching lookup record to each record; the lookup data comes over an info link
  db.lookup           Database Lookup    Adds the columns of the matching row of a database table to each record
transforms / output
  core.log         Log               Writes records to the run log and passes them on
  csv.output       CSV Output        Writes records to a CSV file and passes them on
  db.table-output  Table Output      Inserts each record as a new row into a database table
  db.upsert        Insert or Update  Updates the row with the same keys in a database table, or inserts the record as a new row
  excel.output     Excel Output      Writes records to a sheet of an Excel workbook (.xlsx) and passes them on
  http.response    HTTP Response     Answers the caller of an HTTP trigger with the records as JSON and passes them on
  json.output      JSON Output       Writes records to a JSON or NDJSON file and passes them on
  xml.output       XML Output        Writes records as elements of an XML file and passes them on
